; A single-type tag wrapper whose inner is a range that collapses EXACTLY onto a rust primitive with
; no residual bound (`#6.42(uint .le 255)` -> u8). A ranged inner that *does* carry a residual bound
; (one that doesn't line up with a rust primitive) already wraps to enforce that bound; this fixture
; pins the other half — the exact-collapse case must ALSO wrap, purely so its standalone
; `to/from_cbor_bytes` writes/checks the tag (a transparent `pub type ... = u8` alias would drop the
; tag from the wire). Because the primitive already covers the whole domain there is no bounds check
; to emit: serialize writes `write_tag(42)` then the value, deserialize rejects a wrong tag with
; `DeserializeFailure::TagMismatch`.
tagged_ranged = #6.42(uint .le 255)
